  "body": "I'd like to raise this topic again. I don't want to re-litigate #777, the context in that issue is sufficient. However, as I mentioned in https://github.com/w3cping/privacy-request/issues/49#issuecomment-909819059, there is not justification for entirely leaving out the Security and Privacy Considerations sections. At a minimum, the spec can include `There are no known security impacts of the features in this specification.` as stated in the  [Self-Review Questionnaire](https://www.w3.org/TR/security-privacy-questionnaire/#considerations).\r\n\r\nIf there has not been a full review of the spec for privacy/security, then I encourage doing that, either within WHATWG or in coordination with the W3C PING/TAG, for completeness.",
